WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.225 --> 00:00:01.601
- Today we're gonna talk about

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.805
the two keys to getting A's in law school

00:00:03.805 --> 00:00:05.244
and why most students miss

00:00:05.244 --> 00:00:09.248
the single most important
opportunity that they have.

00:00:09.248 --> 00:00:13.153
(soft instrumental music)

00:00:13.153 --> 00:00:16.556
So if you're a law student,
you think you're in law school,

00:00:16.556 --> 00:00:19.458
but actually you're in essay school.

00:00:19.458 --> 00:00:21.894
That's because almost
all of your final grades

00:00:21.894 --> 00:00:25.287
will be based on
issue-spotting-exam essays.

00:00:25.287 --> 00:00:27.877
So what are the things that you need to do

00:00:27.877 --> 00:00:31.598
in order to ace your
issue-spotting-essay exams?

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:34.382
Well I think there are two
things that you should do.

00:00:34.382 --> 00:00:36.792
The first thing is, the
one that everyone does,

00:00:36.792 --> 00:00:39.151
it's the most obvious thing
that you can do in law school

00:00:39.151 --> 00:00:41.242
and that's master the law.

00:00:41.242 --> 00:00:43.376
Everybody knows this,
if you go to law school

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:44.928
you have to master the law.

00:00:44.928 --> 00:00:46.691
If you go into a contracts class

00:00:46.691 --> 00:00:48.801
you need to master the law of contracts.

00:00:48.801 --> 00:00:50.354
If you go into a property class

00:00:50.354 --> 00:00:52.680
you need to master the law of property.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.895
Learning the substantive
law is the table-stakes

00:00:55.895 --> 00:00:59.290
in law school, it's
necessary but not sufficient.

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:01.399
And to most people's surprise,

00:01:01.399 --> 00:01:03.267
the person who knows the most law

00:01:03.267 --> 00:01:05.079
is not necessarily the person

00:01:05.079 --> 00:01:07.393
that's going to get the
best grade on the exam.

00:01:07.393 --> 00:01:08.870
In fact, far from it.

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:10.287
The person who studies the hardest

00:01:10.287 --> 00:01:12.682
and works the hardest is not necessarily

00:01:12.682 --> 00:01:14.377
the person that's going
to get the best grade.

00:01:14.377 --> 00:01:16.266
In fact they almost never do.

00:01:16.266 --> 00:01:18.591
Everyone is going to
have to learn the law,

00:01:18.591 --> 00:01:21.934
but learning the law itself is not enough.

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:23.667
That'll get you through the door,

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:25.704
but that won't get you an A on the exam.

00:01:25.704 --> 00:01:28.078
The second thing that you have to do

00:01:28.078 --> 00:01:30.119
in order to ace you law school exam

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:33.137
is the thing that so few people do.

00:01:33.137 --> 00:01:36.952
And that's that you
have to master the test.

00:01:36.952 --> 00:01:39.257
In other words you have to learn

00:01:39.257 --> 00:01:42.865
how to write a good law school essay.

00:01:42.865 --> 00:01:45.328
Learning how to take a
law-school-essay exam

00:01:45.328 --> 00:01:46.970
is not a dark art.

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:48.892
There is a science to it.

00:01:48.892 --> 00:01:50.494
It's a skill.

00:01:50.494 --> 00:01:53.473
And any skill can be learned over time,

00:01:53.473 --> 00:01:56.631
just like learning the
piano or playing guitar.

00:01:56.631 --> 00:01:58.470
You'll get better the more you do it

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:00.541
and there are strategies
that will allow you

00:02:00.541 --> 00:02:02.912
to learn how to do it faster.

00:02:02.912 --> 00:02:05.780
The worst thing that you can
possibly do in law school

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:07.820
is to never take a practice test

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:10.638
until the day of your first final exam.

00:02:10.638 --> 00:02:12.340
Now first, let me issue a disclaimer,

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:14.538
many people say that it is impossible

00:02:14.538 --> 00:02:18.798
to improve your skills on
a law school final exam.

00:02:18.798 --> 00:02:20.707
Now to those people I say good luck.

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:22.753
It's so odd to me that the same people

00:02:22.753 --> 00:02:25.930
that spent $2,000 on an LSAT prep-course

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:28.047
and learned how to take the LSAT,

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:29.599
turn around and say that it's impossible

00:02:29.599 --> 00:02:31.749
to get better at law school exams.

00:02:31.749 --> 00:02:34.043
There are so many people, myself included,

00:02:34.043 --> 00:02:36.450
who learned the strategies for logic games

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:38.212
and reading comprehension on the LSAT

00:02:38.212 --> 00:02:40.528
and improved their LSAT
scores dramatically.

00:02:40.528 --> 00:02:42.987
And it's the same in law school.

00:02:42.987 --> 00:02:44.465
Personally I would take the person

00:02:44.465 --> 00:02:47.145
who has practiced the hell
out of issue-spotting exams

00:02:47.145 --> 00:02:49.593
over the person who
has memorized every law

00:02:49.593 --> 00:02:52.096
in contracts or torts or property.

00:02:52.096 --> 00:02:54.429
And the hidden benefit of
learning the strategies

00:02:54.429 --> 00:02:57.502
of how to take a law-school-essay exam

00:02:57.502 --> 00:02:59.422
is that it shapes the way that you study

00:02:59.422 --> 00:03:01.211
throughout the entire semester.

00:03:01.211 --> 00:03:02.684
You study the right things,

00:03:02.684 --> 00:03:04.866
the things that are
going to be on the test.

00:03:04.866 --> 00:03:08.469
Because you get a feeling
for what can be tested

00:03:08.469 --> 00:03:10.852
and it's strange but not
everything you learn in class

00:03:10.852 --> 00:03:12.166
can be tested.

00:03:12.166 --> 00:03:14.027
For example issue-spotting exams

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:17.868
tend to test causes of
actions in lawsuits.

00:03:17.868 --> 00:03:21.114
So they're not well suited for
testing the philosophy of law

00:03:21.114 --> 00:03:23.331
or questions of policy.

00:03:23.331 --> 00:03:25.298
Then plus you learn the law better

00:03:25.298 --> 00:03:27.584
through application.

00:03:27.584 --> 00:03:29.259
If you had enough practice tests

00:03:29.259 --> 00:03:31.407
you could conceivably
learn the entire class

00:03:31.407 --> 00:03:32.849
through the answers to those tests

00:03:32.849 --> 00:03:35.117
without actually having to study.

00:03:35.117 --> 00:03:38.313
Believe me, once you miss a
question on a practice test

00:03:38.313 --> 00:03:40.549
you're not likely to
miss that question again,

00:03:40.549 --> 00:03:42.162
when you see it on the next test

00:03:42.162 --> 00:03:44.619
and maybe that next
test is your final exam.

00:03:44.619 --> 00:03:45.826
So that raises the question,

00:03:45.826 --> 00:03:47.716
why don't more people do this?

00:03:47.716 --> 00:03:50.954
Why do so many people
focus on the law only

00:03:50.954 --> 00:03:54.721
and miss out on the second
key to acing their exam?

00:03:54.721 --> 00:03:56.594
Well most people think law school essays

00:03:56.594 --> 00:03:58.799
are just like undergrad essays.

00:03:58.799 --> 00:04:01.431
If you put off taking practice exams

00:04:01.431 --> 00:04:05.676
and at least looking at
a sample law school exam

00:04:05.676 --> 00:04:07.342
you might not even know

00:04:07.342 --> 00:04:10.410
that a law school exam
is very, very different

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:12.090
from an undergrad essay.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:13.971
And if you don't know that it's different

00:04:13.971 --> 00:04:15.180
you might not even know

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:18.226
that it's a skill that is
worth honing over time.

00:04:18.226 --> 00:04:20.089
And of course let's not forget

00:04:20.089 --> 00:04:22.561
that there is so much information

00:04:22.561 --> 00:04:24.775
about the substantive
law that you're learning.

00:04:24.775 --> 00:04:28.735
Every semester you're probably
in three core classes.

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:30.875
And each one of those
classes is teaching things

00:04:30.875 --> 00:04:32.639
that you've never heard before.

00:04:32.639 --> 00:04:35.468
So there's always more time to study

00:04:35.468 --> 00:04:38.342
the law itself and it is far too easy

00:04:38.342 --> 00:04:40.049
to just put off practice tests

00:04:40.049 --> 00:04:42.577
and put off learning
the strategies of essays

00:04:42.577 --> 00:04:45.017
until much, much later in the semester.

00:04:45.017 --> 00:04:47.787
For a lot of people perfect
is the enemy of good

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:49.707
and they keep trying to get perfect

00:04:49.707 --> 00:04:51.687
at knowing the substantive law

00:04:51.687 --> 00:04:53.945
without even trying to learn

00:04:53.945 --> 00:04:57.615
the basics of writing
issue-spotting exams.

00:04:57.615 --> 00:05:00.267
As a result they never
learn how to spot the issues

00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:03.007
and they never learn how
to write those good essays,

00:05:03.007 --> 00:05:05.411
the ones that will get A's on the exam.

00:05:05.411 --> 00:05:07.401
But don't be like those other students.

00:05:07.401 --> 00:05:09.497
Know that there are two keys

00:05:09.497 --> 00:05:11.280
to getting A's on your final exam.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:13.676
One is of course learning
the substantive law,

00:05:13.676 --> 00:05:17.574
but the other is learning
to master the test itself.

00:05:17.574 --> 00:05:19.486
In another video we'll explain the tactics

00:05:19.486 --> 00:05:21.628
for how you can start
taking practice exams

00:05:21.628 --> 00:05:23.577
months before the finals
and the strategies

00:05:23.577 --> 00:05:25.043
that going into spotting issues

00:05:25.043 --> 00:05:27.379
and writing those A-worthy exams.

